---

<BaseLayout
  title="How I made $4,700 in one month trading crypto"
  description="A September 2024 case study of the high-risk DCA trend continuation strategy I used to 2x my crypto trading account."
  wide
>
  <article class="page-stack writing-article finance-article">
    <nav class="finance-rail" aria-label="Article sections" data-finance-rail>
      <ol>
        {
          sections.map(({ id, label }, index) => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={`#${id}`}
                aria-label={label}
                data-section-link={id}
                data-state={index === 0 ? "active" : "pending"}
              >
                <span class="finance-rail-mark" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span class="finance-rail-label">{label}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <header class="article-header">
      <a class="back-link" href="/finance">Finance</a>
      <div class="article-heading">
        <p class="article-kicker">Case study · September 2024</p>
        <h1>How I made $4,700 in one month trading crypto</h1>
        <p class="article-deck">
          The high-risk DCA trend continuation strategy I used to 2× my account
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="finance-results" aria-label="Results shown in the supplied trading screenshots">
        <div>
          <dt>Cumulative P&amp;L</dt>
          <dd>+$4,712.60</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Account return</dt>
          <dd>+114.45%</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Closed positions</dt>
          <dd>20</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Recorded win rate</dt>
          <dd>100%</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <p class="finance-proof-link">
        <a href="/finance/dca-trend-continuation/bybit-proof">
          View the Bybit proof →
        </a>
      </p>

      <aside class="article-note finance-risk-note">
        <p>
          This is one month of personal results, not an expected return. I traded leveraged crypto
          derivatives and risked roughly 20% to 30% of my account when margin allowed. A short
          losing streak at that size can destroy an account. This article is educational, not
          financial advice.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <div class="article-body">
      <section id="strategy-overview" aria-labelledby="strategy-overview-heading">
        <p class="article-kicker">01</p>
        <h2 id="strategy-overview-heading">Strategy overview</h2>
        <p>
          The setup trades a pullback in an established trend. In an uptrend, price forms higher
          highs and higher lows, then pulls back before continuing. A downtrend flips that pattern.
          I wait for the market to show direction, then try to join that direction during the
          pullback.
        </p>
        <p>
          "DCA" here means scaling into one leveraged position with three planned limit orders. It
          is not the usual long-term practice of buying a fixed dollar amount on a schedule.
        </p>
        <ul class="article-list">
          <li>Uptrend: buy a pullback after a significant previous high breaks.</li>
          <li>Downtrend: sell a bounce after a significant previous low breaks.</li>
          <li>Do not enter until trend, wave position, and EMA alignment agree.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Orientation examples:
          <a href="https://www.tradingview.com/x/7GjQCPLz/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
            >long continuation ↗</a
          > and
          <a href="https://www.tradingview.com/x/p5yMICJu/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
            >short continuation ↗</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="dca-method" aria-labelledby="dca-method-heading">
        <p class="article-kicker">02</p>
        <h2 id="dca-method-heading">The three-limit-order method</h2>
        <p>
          I plot a Fibonacci template across the impulse and stage entries at 0.618, 0.382, and
          0.17. Each deeper order is larger. The stop stays at -0.05 while the profit target moves
          closer as more orders fill.
        </p>

        <div class="strategy-table-wrap wide-block">
          <table class="strategy-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Order</th>
                <th scope="col">Entry</th>
                <th scope="col">Size</th>
                <th scope="col">Take profit</th>
                <th scope="col">Stop</th>
                <th scope="col">Risk ratio used</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Limit 1</th>
                <td>0.618</td>
                <td>1×</td>
                <td>1.272</td>
                <td>-0.05</td>
                <td>1:1</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Limit 2</th>
                <td>0.382</td>
                <td>3×</td>
                <td>Just below 0.618</td>
                <td>-0.05</td>
                <td>3:1</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Limit 3</th>
                <td>0.17</td>
                <td>5×</td>
                <td>Just below 0.382</td>
                <td>-0.05</td>
                <td>5:1</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>
          The 3× and 5× orders pull the average entry toward the deeper retracement. They also make
          the position much larger exactly when price has moved farther against the initial entry.
          All three orders, targets, and the final stop must be calculated before the first fill.
        </p>

        <div class="diagram-grid wide-block">
          {
            limitOrderDiagrams.map(({ image, title, alt }) => (
              <figure class="finance-figure">
                <button
                  class="image-viewer-trigger"
                  type="button"
                  data-viewer-trigger
                  data-full-src={image.src}
                  data-full-alt={alt}
                  data-full-caption={title}
                  aria-label={`Open ${title.toLowerCase()} diagram at full size`}
